    {
      "id": "p0076-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The Japanese language has three different writing systems: hiragana, katakana, and kanji. In standard written Japanese, these three systems work together to convey information. There are approximately 50 hiragana characters, 50 katakana characters, and 2000 standard kanji characters.",
        "raw": "The Japanese language has three different writing systems: hiragana, katakana,\nand kanji. In standard written Japanese, these three systems work together\nto convey information. There are approximately 50 hiragana characters, 50\nkatakana characters, and 2000 standard kanji characters.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
