    {
      "id": "p0076-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Because Toby designed Undertale as a love letter to retro Japanese RPGs, he asked 8-4 to mimic the retro style of classic Japanese games, particularly when characters speak. For this reason, the Japanese dialogue in Undertale uses this simplified writing style, while inanimate objects like plaques and signs use the more standard writing style.",
        "raw": "Because Toby designed Undertale as a love letter to retro Japanese RPGs, he\nasked 8-4 to mimic the retro style of classic Japanese games, particularly when\ncharacters speak. For this reason, the Japanese dialogue in Undertale uses this\nsimplified writing style, while inanimate objects like plaques and signs use the\nmore standard writing style.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29504474,
          0.65403571,
          0.89921928,
          0.73995714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29004484,
          0.65332143,
          0.90532688,
          0.74102857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          32,
          33,
          34,
          35,
          36
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Toby 把 Undertale 当作献给复古日式角色扮演游戏的情书，因此请 8-4 模仿经典日本游戏的写法，尤其是角色说话时。所以，日语对白采用这种简化写法，铭牌、标牌等无生命物体则使用更标准的写法。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
